WEBVTT

00:00:53.596 --> 00:00:55.723
Good morning.

00:00:55.932 --> 00:00:57.850
You're alone today?

00:00:58.059 --> 00:01:00.520
Oh... Yeah.

00:01:01.646 --> 00:01:03.022
See ya.

00:01:09.821 --> 00:01:13.825
"14 Days Until the 32nd Sports Festival"

00:01:16.411 --> 00:01:18.830
Whoa. So--

00:01:26.087 --> 00:01:29.382
Asumi-senpai.

00:01:29.924 --> 00:01:32.343
S-Sorry.

00:01:32.552 --> 00:01:34.387
It's fine.

00:02:02.624 --> 00:02:03.625
I gotta stand up now

00:02:03.625 --> 00:02:05.293
"Convenience Store Boy Friends"
I gotta stand up now

00:02:05.293 --> 00:02:06.127
"Convenience Store Boy Friends"

00:02:06.127 --> 00:02:07.128
"Convenience Store Boy Friends"
A devil with the face of an angel--feel so bad

00:02:07.128 --> 00:02:12.550
A devil with the face of an angel--feel so bad

00:02:12.759 --> 00:02:18.389
I lift my face; sighs don't suit me

00:02:18.598 --> 00:02:19.641
Damn it

00:02:19.849 --> 00:02:23.728
Someone's voice asks, "How's everyone doing?"

00:02:23.936 --> 00:02:26.439
How we do right now, hey hey hey

00:02:26.648 --> 00:02:31.402
I can't stand up yet--right:
get moving by confronting it head-on

00:02:31.611 --> 00:02:32.779
The deciding touchdown!

00:02:32.987 --> 00:02:35.990
One, two, come on!
Kick it to the curb

00:02:36.199 --> 00:02:39.702
Third-day troubles--no sweat!
We're gonna make you say

00:02:39.911 --> 00:02:42.080
Yeah, yeah, yeah

00:02:42.288 --> 00:02:43.039
Let me hear you say

00:02:43.247 --> 00:02:44.999
Yeah, yeah, yeah

00:02:45.208 --> 00:02:46.959
I gotta stand up now

00:02:47.168 --> 00:02:50.380
Oh, more laughs tonight

00:02:50.588 --> 00:02:53.675
Life is the best--c'mon, face up now

00:02:53.883 --> 00:02:58.638
Oh, more laughs tonight--take life face up

00:02:58.846 --> 00:03:01.766
I gotta stand up now

00:03:01.974 --> 00:03:04.852
One, two, come on! Kick it to the curb

00:03:05.061 --> 00:03:08.606
Third-day troubles--no sweat!
We're gonna make you say

00:03:08.815 --> 00:03:11.401
Yeah, yeah, yeah

00:03:12.694 --> 00:03:15.863
Oh, I gotta stand up now

00:03:16.072 --> 00:03:19.367
Oh, I gotta stand up now

00:03:19.575 --> 00:03:22.704
Oh, I gotta stand up now

00:03:22.912 --> 00:03:26.708
Oh, I gotta stand up now

00:03:28.668 --> 00:03:33.756
"June"

00:03:34.298 --> 00:03:36.467
That's all for today.

00:03:36.676 --> 00:03:38.428
Stand.

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:41.222
Bow.

00:03:47.812 --> 00:03:49.272
Haruki.

00:03:49.856 --> 00:03:52.608
Hey, you should've told
me you were gonna be late.

00:03:52.817 --> 00:03:54.318
Calm down and listen.

00:03:54.527 --> 00:03:56.028
What?

00:03:56.237 --> 00:03:56.988
Hey.

00:03:57.196 --> 00:03:59.824
I'll tell you everything I saw.

00:04:00.032 --> 00:04:01.492
What?

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:42.283
Mashiki was with a guy?

00:04:42.492 --> 00:04:45.453
It seemed like she's known him a while.

00:04:45.661 --> 00:04:47.747
They were having a friendly conversation.

00:04:47.955 --> 00:04:51.125
--Really?
--"Really"? What kind of reaction is that?

00:04:51.334 --> 00:04:53.127
You have such an ambiguous attitude.

00:04:53.336 --> 00:04:57.673
I'll say it again, but
Mashiki isn't like that.

00:04:57.882 --> 00:04:59.926
Keep your delusions under control.

00:05:00.134 --> 00:05:01.052
You're not very honest.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:03.596
It's not like that.
Go back to your class.

00:05:03.805 --> 00:05:05.681
Oh, really? Forget it, then.

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:07.433
Bye.

00:05:13.940 --> 00:05:16.150
He's sulking.

00:05:38.422 --> 00:05:40.800
What's his problem?

00:05:41.008 --> 00:05:42.885
Class rep, what do you think?

00:05:43.094 --> 00:05:44.846
Keep your voice down.

00:05:45.054 --> 00:05:48.850
But there's no one else here. Who cares?

00:05:49.058 --> 00:05:51.185
You're not going to work?

00:05:51.394 --> 00:05:53.813
Then why don't you go to practice?

00:06:04.031 --> 00:06:05.825
It's his problem.

00:06:06.033 --> 00:06:07.034
Yeah, but...

00:06:07.243 --> 00:06:09.912
Leave him be. You're being nosy.

00:06:10.121 --> 00:06:11.622
I'm sure you're bothering Mashiki-san, too.

00:06:11.831 --> 00:06:13.749
You're so mean.

00:06:16.127 --> 00:06:17.837
There. That's him!

00:06:18.045 --> 00:06:19.755
What?

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:25.052
What's wrong?

00:06:25.261 --> 00:06:26.679
Sorry. I'll be right back.

00:06:26.888 --> 00:06:29.223
What? Honda-kun?

00:06:36.564 --> 00:06:38.024
Hey, wait!

00:06:38.232 --> 00:06:41.027
Can't you hear us?

00:06:41.235 --> 00:06:42.737
Should we get a teacher?

00:06:42.945 --> 00:06:44.238
| don't think that's a good idea.

00:06:44.447 --> 00:06:46.908
But at this rate...

00:06:54.832 --> 00:06:57.877
Don't make us say it again!

00:07:00.046 --> 00:07:04.425
Just because your times are pretty good
doesn't mean you get special treatment.

00:07:04.634 --> 00:07:06.802
We have new members joining the team.

00:07:07.011 --> 00:07:09.263
We need you to serve as an example for them.

00:07:09.472 --> 00:07:11.641
They don't need an example.

00:07:11.849 --> 00:07:13.559
What?

00:07:13.768 --> 00:07:17.521
| don't run to make friends.

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:19.023
What?

00:07:19.231 --> 00:07:21.567
You're still saying that?

00:07:21.776 --> 00:07:25.488
It's a senior's responsibility
to look after his underclassmen!

00:07:25.696 --> 00:07:28.407
We're telling you to be a team player.

00:07:28.616 --> 00:07:31.661
No one will follow you with that attitude.

00:07:31.869 --> 00:07:33.329
| seriously can't believe this guy.

00:07:33.537 --> 00:07:36.290
Asumi, you're a brat!

00:07:36.499 --> 00:07:40.169
E-Excuse me, coming through.

00:07:41.587 --> 00:07:43.381
Hurry up.

00:07:47.843 --> 00:07:49.637
I'm sorry.

00:07:52.556 --> 00:07:53.849
Are you okay?

00:07:54.058 --> 00:07:57.061
Huh? Thank you.

00:08:00.773 --> 00:08:02.149
Damn it.

00:08:02.358 --> 00:08:05.361
Sorry. We'll get this cleaned up in no time.

00:08:05.569 --> 00:08:07.446
Hurry up!

00:08:08.489 --> 00:08:09.782
Here.

00:08:09.991 --> 00:08:11.909
Oh...

00:08:12.118 --> 00:08:13.744
Thank you.

00:08:13.953 --> 00:08:14.954
What are you doing?

00:08:15.162 --> 00:08:17.164
You're blocking the walkway.

00:08:17.373 --> 00:08:20.084
Shit. It's the student council president.

00:08:22.628 --> 00:08:26.215
Librarian, you can go.

00:08:26.424 --> 00:08:30.011
Tell us what happened.

00:08:30.219 --> 00:08:32.596
You, too, Mishima Haruki-kun.

00:08:32.805 --> 00:08:34.682
What?

00:08:34.890 --> 00:08:36.392
Aw...

00:08:43.649 --> 00:08:45.317
What are you doing?

00:08:45.526 --> 00:08:49.655
| finished the rest.
I'm going to turn them in.

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:53.826
He's here. Mashiki's...

00:08:54.035 --> 00:08:56.162
Excuse me!

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:58.497
You two.

00:09:01.584 --> 00:09:04.003
Eat up!

00:09:04.211 --> 00:09:05.129
Wow.

00:09:05.337 --> 00:09:06.797
This looks good.

00:09:07.006 --> 00:09:09.800
Uh, is this the cooking club or something?

00:09:10.009 --> 00:09:11.510
Wow, can you tell?

00:09:11.719 --> 00:09:16.015
We're actually not as cool as a club.
We're just a student society.

00:09:16.223 --> 00:09:18.225
We have only two members.

00:09:18.434 --> 00:09:20.644
That's why we kidnap food tasters

00:09:20.853 --> 00:09:23.689
to spread the word and recruit more members.

00:09:23.898 --> 00:09:25.066
Right?

00:09:29.153 --> 00:09:30.613
Who's he?

00:09:30.821 --> 00:09:31.447
Nasa-kun?

00:09:31.655 --> 00:09:32.948
Nasa?

00:09:33.157 --> 00:09:34.575
Sanagi Nasa-kun.

00:09:34.784 --> 00:09:36.660
He's a great cook and our club president.

00:09:36.869 --> 00:09:38.537
It's not like that.

00:09:38.746 --> 00:09:40.998
It is.

00:09:42.833 --> 00:09:46.170
Did Mashiki fall in love with his cooking?

00:09:46.378 --> 00:09:47.588
Maybe.

00:09:47.797 --> 00:09:50.424
You're welcome to have this, too.

00:09:50.633 --> 00:09:51.926
Well, I'm gonna go.

00:09:52.134 --> 00:09:53.928
--What?
--Okay.

00:09:56.889 --> 00:09:58.766
Bye-bye.

00:09:59.517 --> 00:10:02.478
W-We have something to do, too.

00:10:02.686 --> 00:10:04.188
--Bye.
--What?

00:10:04.396 --> 00:10:05.523
--Right?
--What?

00:10:05.731 --> 00:10:06.607
Come on.

00:10:06.816 --> 00:10:07.942
Let's go.

00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:10.319
What? But you're not finished.

00:10:10.528 --> 00:10:11.445
Sorry.

00:10:11.654 --> 00:10:13.739
What? Hey, wait.

00:10:13.948 --> 00:10:16.659
Really? Too bad.

00:10:16.867 --> 00:10:18.702
Th-Thanks for the food.

00:10:18.911 --> 00:10:20.704
Come again.

00:10:21.789 --> 00:10:22.706
"Student Council"

00:10:22.706 --> 00:10:24.959
"Student Council"
We talked to the third-years.

00:10:24.959 --> 00:10:25.167
"Student Council"

00:10:25.167 --> 00:10:27.837
It's exactly what I expected.

00:10:28.045 --> 00:10:32.091
Though they're probably nervous as
well with their last meet coming up.

00:10:32.299 --> 00:10:35.845
You do stand out in all kinds of ways.

00:10:36.053 --> 00:10:37.388
Sorry.

00:10:37.596 --> 00:10:38.889
We're sorry, too.

00:10:39.098 --> 00:10:39.932
What?

00:10:40.141 --> 00:10:41.725
You got caught up in their argument, right?

00:10:41.934 --> 00:10:45.646
The track-and-field club's
quarrels are nothing new.

00:10:45.855 --> 00:10:49.483
You just got caught in the
crossfire, first-year.

00:10:51.569 --> 00:10:54.697
I'm sure you have lots to say as well,

00:10:54.905 --> 00:10:57.741
but since you've caused a commotion,
you'll both be punished.

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:01.078
I'll come up with their punishment later.

00:11:01.287 --> 00:11:06.250
Asumi, as punishment, I'm requiring
you to help run the sports festival.

00:11:06.458 --> 00:11:08.544
What? Me?

00:11:08.752 --> 00:11:09.920
We don't have enough volunteers.

00:11:10.129 --> 00:11:11.547
Aren't you being a little pushy?

00:11:11.755 --> 00:11:15.634
No one will help unless I am.

00:11:15.843 --> 00:11:17.094
What about Waka-chan?

00:11:17.303 --> 00:11:19.096
I'm not counting her.

00:11:19.305 --> 00:11:21.182
| see.

00:11:22.892 --> 00:11:26.145
You can come during lunch,
after school, or after practice.

00:11:26.353 --> 00:11:30.024
Every day you'll come here and help us.

00:11:30.232 --> 00:11:31.233
Got it?

00:11:31.442 --> 00:11:32.401
Okay.

00:11:32.610 --> 00:11:35.112
Anyway, we'll be counting on you, too.

00:11:35.321 --> 00:11:36.405
Okay.

00:11:36.614 --> 00:11:38.741
What? Me, too?

00:11:38.949 --> 00:11:40.075
Of course.

00:11:40.284 --> 00:11:43.120
I'll talk to the swim team for you.

00:11:43.329 --> 00:11:46.290
Okay, go lend a hand.

00:11:46.498 --> 00:11:49.126
There's still a mountain of work left to do.

00:11:49.335 --> 00:11:50.753
You'll be busy.

00:11:50.961 --> 00:11:54.048
I'm gonna go wrap up that other matter.

00:11:54.256 --> 00:11:58.093
Sure. I'll head to the faculty office, then.

00:11:58.302 --> 00:12:02.598
You two can ask the vice
president for instructions.

00:12:16.403 --> 00:12:18.239
The hospital again?

00:12:18.447 --> 00:12:20.741
Why am I doing this with you?

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:22.284
You've already come this far.

00:12:22.493 --> 00:12:23.994
You dragged me into this.

00:12:24.203 --> 00:12:26.580
I'm doing this for Mashiki, too.

00:12:26.789 --> 00:12:28.582
| want to make sure her
boyfriend's a decent guy.

00:12:28.791 --> 00:12:30.834
| need to see it with my own eyes.

00:12:31.043 --> 00:12:34.213
Why are real boys so stupid?

00:12:34.421 --> 00:12:36.131
He turned the corner.

00:12:53.649 --> 00:12:56.235
Can I ask you something?

00:12:56.443 --> 00:13:01.240
What were you doing at the
hospital this morning?

00:13:01.448 --> 00:13:04.702
| had to drop off something.

00:13:13.752 --> 00:13:15.796
Uh-oh. Run for it.

00:13:16.005 --> 00:13:17.881
H-Hey.

00:13:19.174 --> 00:13:21.552
What are you doing?

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:23.637
Um...

00:13:48.245 --> 00:13:49.580
Your face...

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:53.500
Are you okay?

00:13:54.960 --> 00:14:01.342
Seems as though the track-and-field
team has a lot going on.

00:14:01.550 --> 00:14:03.302
Sounds rough.

00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:07.556
Not really. I just run.

00:14:09.892 --> 00:14:12.644
"Just run," huh?

00:14:14.521 --> 00:14:19.360
| just swim, too. I understand what you mean.

00:14:19.568 --> 00:14:21.362
What's your time?

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:24.073
My freestyle's around 23-24.

00:14:24.281 --> 00:14:25.115
That's impressive.

00:14:25.324 --> 00:14:27.493
There are faster guys.

00:14:27.701 --> 00:14:30.371
| don't really care about my times.

00:14:30.579 --> 00:14:32.664
You don't care?

00:14:32.873 --> 00:14:37.753
| just like being in the water.

00:14:37.961 --> 00:14:40.339
Really? Sounds nice.

00:14:40.547 --> 00:14:42.299
What?

00:14:42.508 --> 00:14:46.095
| don't think about
anything when I'm running.

00:14:46.303 --> 00:14:49.473
| just feel the breeze in front of me.

00:14:49.681 --> 00:14:51.809
Sounds nice.

00:14:53.102 --> 00:14:56.605
Okay, that's enough for today, you two.

00:14:56.814 --> 00:14:57.898
Thanks for your help.

00:14:58.107 --> 00:14:59.274
Goodbye.

00:14:59.483 --> 00:15:00.901
Goodbye.

00:15:01.110 --> 00:15:04.029
See you tomorrow.

00:15:22.214 --> 00:15:24.216
"Library"

00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:38.105
Jeez.

00:15:38.313 --> 00:15:40.524
It's raining.

00:15:46.363 --> 00:15:48.740
Be careful on your way home.

00:15:50.242 --> 00:15:51.368
What? Don't you have an umbrella?

00:15:51.577 --> 00:15:54.955
I'm taking the bus. Bye.

00:15:55.164 --> 00:15:57.166
See you later.

00:16:16.977 --> 00:16:18.854
Welcome.

00:16:24.568 --> 00:16:26.695
Let's see.

00:16:35.913 --> 00:16:36.914
"55cm Plastic Umbrellas”
"Sold Out"

00:16:36.914 --> 00:16:39.917
"60cm Automatic Umbrellas"

00:16:44.129 --> 00:16:45.380
I'd like this, please.

00:16:45.589 --> 00:16:47.090
Thank you.

00:16:47.299 --> 00:16:48.550
Sorry about that.

00:16:48.759 --> 00:16:52.554
Once it started raining,
we sold out in a heartbeat.

00:16:52.763 --> 00:16:55.224
That will be 540 yen.

00:16:55.432 --> 00:16:58.810
You'll be using this right away, right?

00:16:59.019 --> 00:17:01.021
Oh, actually...

00:17:04.775 --> 00:17:06.944
Hello.

00:17:18.121 --> 00:17:20.624
Thanks. I promise I'll pay you back tomorrow.

00:17:20.832 --> 00:17:22.793
Anytime is fine.

00:17:23.001 --> 00:17:25.462
Have you been volunteering this whole time?

00:17:25.671 --> 00:17:27.089
Yeah.

00:17:27.297 --> 00:17:29.132
That sounds fun.

00:17:29.341 --> 00:17:30.092
Really?

00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:32.052
The handicraft club is doing it, too.

00:17:32.261 --> 00:17:34.555
Did you see the banner near the school gate?

00:17:34.763 --> 00:17:36.223
That huge thing?

00:17:36.431 --> 00:17:40.727
Yeah. We're making flags for the cheer
squad and balls for the ball-toss, too.

00:17:40.936 --> 00:17:42.604
Really? That's impressive.

00:17:42.813 --> 00:17:44.523
Wait, a ball-toss?

00:17:44.731 --> 00:17:46.316
| thought the same thing.

00:17:46.525 --> 00:17:50.487
High schoolers seem too old for a ball-toss.

00:17:50.696 --> 00:17:52.114
Oh, sorry.

00:17:52.322 --> 00:17:54.658
It's fine.

00:17:55.492 --> 00:17:57.327
Mishima-kun, I bet you'll stand out.

00:17:57.536 --> 00:18:01.039
--Huh?
--At the sports festival. You're athletic.

00:18:01.248 --> 00:18:04.126
| don't know about that.
I'm okay in the water.

00:18:04.334 --> 00:18:06.253
You stood out during middle school, too.

00:18:06.461 --> 00:18:08.839
That's because the other guys were, well...

00:18:09.047 --> 00:18:13.427
What? Mashiki, when you
say middle school, I...

00:18:15.762 --> 00:18:19.016
Uh, er... Right.

00:18:35.991 --> 00:18:37.701
Hey, listen.

00:18:41.204 --> 00:18:43.123
Nothing.

00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:50.088
Hey.

00:18:55.052 --> 00:18:57.054
"Loser"

00:19:02.559 --> 00:19:03.727
--Wait.
--Huh?

00:19:03.935 --> 00:19:05.437
Don't move.

00:19:16.823 --> 00:19:17.449
What?

00:19:17.658 --> 00:19:19.618
Don't move.

00:19:20.535 --> 00:19:21.870
Okay.

00:19:22.079 --> 00:19:25.832
If you don't clean it
right away, it'll stain.

00:19:35.467 --> 00:19:37.052
Thanks.

00:19:44.851 --> 00:19:48.146
D-Does the guy you're seeing not mind?

00:19:48.355 --> 00:19:49.523
What do you mean?

00:19:49.731 --> 00:19:54.444
| mean that guy. Your boyfriend or whatever.

00:19:54.653 --> 00:19:55.612
| don't have one!

00:19:55.821 --> 00:19:57.489
What?

00:19:57.698 --> 00:20:00.367
Please, Mishima-kun.
| don't have a boyfriend.

00:20:00.575 --> 00:20:02.452
Don't say things like that.

00:20:02.661 --> 00:20:03.829
All set.

00:20:04.037 --> 00:20:06.039
Thanks.

00:20:32.607 --> 00:20:34.609
Say hi to Mishima-kun for me.

00:20:34.818 --> 00:20:36.695
Where are you headed? I'll take you home.

00:20:36.903 --> 00:20:38.488
Take me home? Who?

00:20:38.697 --> 00:20:39.656
Me.

00:20:39.865 --> 00:20:40.949
Why would you?

00:20:41.158 --> 00:20:41.950
Because...

00:20:42.159 --> 00:20:45.662
Uh, never mind.

00:20:45.871 --> 00:20:46.538
Bye.

00:20:46.747 --> 00:20:50.292
Uh, yeah. See you tomorrow.

00:21:01.094 --> 00:21:01.762
Hello?

00:21:01.970 --> 00:21:04.890
You finally answered! Good news!

00:21:05.098 --> 00:21:06.183
You should be thanking me.

00:21:06.391 --> 00:21:09.561
Me and the class rep spent
all day doing research.

00:21:09.770 --> 00:21:11.271
What? Researching what?

00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:13.356
Mashiki's guy.

00:21:13.565 --> 00:21:17.235
I'm just here to see a doctor
who took care of me before.

00:21:17.444 --> 00:21:21.281
I've run into Mashiki-san at
this hospital a few times.

00:21:21.490 --> 00:21:23.158
We're just acquaintances.

00:21:23.366 --> 00:21:24.534
That's what he said.

00:21:24.743 --> 00:21:29.790
Ahem! So according to our
research, Mashiki's single.

00:21:29.998 --> 00:21:30.707
| know.

00:21:30.916 --> 00:21:32.000
What? How?

00:21:32.209 --> 00:21:36.129
Anyway, did you follow
this Sanagi guy all day?

00:21:36.338 --> 00:21:37.923
Hey, don't be like that!

00:21:38.131 --> 00:21:39.966
| did this for you and Mashiki-chan.

00:21:40.175 --> 00:21:42.260
Ugh, never mind!

00:22:10.455 --> 00:22:18.964
Another city light blinks out

00:22:19.172 --> 00:22:28.807
Seems I'm the only one
being left behind like this

00:22:29.015 --> 00:22:37.524
I leaned in close to the light
of the vending machine

00:22:37.732 --> 00:22:46.658
And bought something
other than my usual coffee

00:22:46.867 --> 00:22:51.329
I wonder if I can be myself

00:22:51.538 --> 00:22:57.377
From now on, and even further beyond

00:22:58.503 --> 00:23:07.470
Surely someday we'll come
to know sadness as love

00:23:07.679 --> 00:23:16.813
Reconnecting somewhere
and parting again, over and over

00:23:17.022 --> 00:23:30.577
Surely the day will come when we're
all too used to feeling joy

00:23:30.785 --> 00:23:37.125
Call that happiness

